    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a pretty strong point. so if the goal of a modern legal system should be progress and healing rather than just being punitive, wouldn't it be fair to say that retributive justice is essentially an obsolete framework that doesn't align with contemporary moral standards?",
