      "content": "While restorative ideals align well with modern goals of healing, labeling retributive justice outright \"obsolete\" is an overstatement. Many modern systems seek a hybrid approach, using retributive elements to establish clear societal boundaries while incorporating restorative practices for rehabilitation. The debate is less about obsolescence and more about finding the optimal *balance* between exacting deserved punishment and fostering genuine repair and preventing future harm.",
      "source": "target",
